Bridge 0137 (B65): converted YCbCr textures hold half the memory. With SWEET_YCBCR_GPU=1 backboardd kept, per IOSurface texture
CoreAnimation holds, an R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT image (16.6 MB at 1080p) plus a plane-sized staging buffer (3.1 MB) for the texture's life;
4 playing tabs took backboardd to 675-740 MB (vs ~430 on the CPU path) and exhausted the 940 MB pool.
1. Lazy staging: YCbCrConversion builds the fast conversion (0131) first; where it takes the texture, the staging buffer, its set and
   copies (now `Staged`) are made only at the first conversion the fast kernel does not take: its surface's buffer rebound to other pages
   (a no-copy HostPages buffer, ShadowBuffer::Rebound, rebind.rs). `ShadowCopies::prepare`, called first thing in Encoder::plan_shadows
   (the hook upstream metal2vulkan 7ef17497 uses for its own lazy `YCbCrConversion::make`), makes it, so a fallback conversion's uses and
   record see it; until then uses() names no staging buffer. Textures without a fast form (10-bit, 4:2:2/4:4:4, over plane 1) make it
   with the texture, as before. Off: SWEET_YCBCR_LAZY=0.
2. RGBA8 output: an 8-bit 4:2:0 layout read converted (YCBCR8_420_2P over 420v/420f; YCbCrCodes::rgba8) is held as R8G8B8A8_UNORM:
   the format repr (metal::format ycbcr_repr, so the image plan, plan.format check and every view agree), the runtime's image_formats,
   both conversion kernels' storage view (Rgba8: ycbcr_convert_module_stored, keyed by a new bool in OwnedModule::YCbCrConvert; the fast
   kernel's per shape) and the binder: such a slot always takes the device's linear filter (0134's arm), since c/255 texels are off the
   1/2048 grid the exact routine sums on. Precision is the CPU path's RGBA8 (a read off Metal's by at most 1/510). 10-bit, sRGB twins
   and extended-range formats keep their images. Default on; SWEET_YCBCR_RGBA8=0 restores Rgba16f (and 0134's switch for 8-bit).
Saving per texture: 1080p 8.3 MB image + 3.1 MB staging (19.7 -> 8.3 MB), 720p 3.7 + 1.4 MB (8.8 -> 3.7 MB).
Not covered: heap (argument buffer) textures keep the exact filter routine (0134), now summing c/255 texels (error under 1/2048).
Reuse: lazy staging follows upstream metal2vulkan 7ef17497 (YCbCrConversion::make / ShadowCopies::prepare at plan_shadows; not
ported whole: its refresh and in-place reads are a different design); no RGBA8 output upstream or in AdrenoMetal (both keep Rgba16f).
Logs "SWEET_YCBCR out rgba8|rgba16f, staging lazy|eager" once per process (/dev/console, /var/local/mtl2.log).

